course: dictionary
lesson: 9737
title: Sunrise and the sky
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Sunrise is a word you can break into two parts: sun and rise. It is the time in the morning when the sun first appears above the edge of the land or sea. «Watch the sunrise from the top of the hill.» Here it means the moment the sun comes up.
explain: Context helps you know which meaning you need. «The stones of Stonehenge line up with the sunrise in midsummer.» Try swapping in "the moment the sun first appears": the sentence still makes sense, so sunrise is a time here. Sometimes it means the colours and light in the sky instead, as in «The sunrise was pink and gold.»
explain: Sunrise has an opposite, sunset. «Sunrise is your side turning towards the Sun; sunset is your side turning away.» Sunrise starts the day and sunset ends it. Two useful phrases are «at sunrise» and «from sunrise to sunset», which means the whole day.
fact: Sunrise means the time in the morning when the sun first appears above the horizon.
fact: A sunrise can also mean the colours and light in the sky when the sun comes up.
fact: The sun seems to rise because the Earth spins, not because the sun moves round the Earth.
fact: Sunrise times change through the year: they are earlier in summer and later in winter.
fact: In stories, a sunrise often means a new start or a little hope.
exercise: «The farmer got up at sunrise to feed the hens.» What does sunrise mean here? | A bright lamp in the farmyard | The time the sun goes down at night | The sky being dark and full of stars | *The time the sun first appears in the morning
exercise: Sunrise times change through the year. When is sunrise earliest? | At midnight | *In summer | In winter | Always at six o'clock
exercise: Which way does the sun rise? | *East | West | North | South
test: «The sunrise was pink and gold over the sea.» Here sunrise means | *The colours and light in the sky as the sun comes up | The start of a holiday | A time on a clock at night | A boat that sails out early
test: In a story, a sunrise often shows | *A new start or a little hope | A storm that will never end | That the characters are lost forever
exam: «From sunrise to sunset, the farmers worked in the fields.» Which word means the moment the sun first appears in the morning? | *sunrise | sunset | horizon | midwinter
